{
  "name": "Jev: incident and alert triage",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Incident and alert triage\nFor every alert Jev picks the **service area**, scores **severity** (SEV4 to SEV1) and says whether it is a **customer-facing outage**.\n\nConfident customer-facing alerts at SEV2 or above page on-call. Other confident alerts become tickets. Unclear alerts go to the on-call channel for a human look.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "42cf9470-6e41-5d58-a5b8-b1ec942ec694",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "f6ebfd22-cee7-5922-ada3-0815c5bb04b9",
      "name": "Try with sample data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Invented sample data. In production, replace this node with your real trigger.\nreturn [\n  {\n    \"source\": \"monitoring\",\n    \"title\": \"Checkout error rate 38% (threshold 2%)\",\n    \"details\": \"payments-api 5xx spike since 09:12 UTC across all regions. Card payments failing for customers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"monitoring\",\n    \"title\": \"Nightly warehouse export 40 min late\",\n    \"details\": \"data-export job still running. Downstream finance dashboard will refresh late. No customer impact.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"support\",\n    \"title\": \"Several customers cannot log in\",\n    \"details\": \"12 tickets in 20 minutes: \\\"invalid session\\\" after login on the web app. Mobile seems fine.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"monitoring\",\n    \"title\": \"Disk 81% on build runner 3\",\n    \"details\": \"ci-runner-3 disk usage crossed 80%. Builds still passing.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"source\": \"chat\",\n    \"title\": \"something feels off\",\n    \"details\": \"A few things look slower than usual? Not sure where.\"\n  }\n].map((json) => ({ json }));"
      },
      "id": "4c926710-86c4-5c5d-a0ae-4261d9c987fb",
      "name": "Sample alerts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "askSeveral",
        "stateSource": "item",
        "questions": {
          "question": [
            {
              "key": "area",
              "type": "choice",
              "instructions": "Which service area does this alert belong to?",
              "criteria": "payments: Checkout, card payments, billing services\nauth: Login, sessions, single sign-on, user accounts\napi: Public API and webhooks\nweb_app: The web or mobile app front end\ndata: Data pipelines, exports, reporting jobs\ninfrastructure: Servers, disks, networks, build and deploy systems",
              "threshold": 0,
              "gate": true
            },
            {
              "key": "severity",
              "type": "score",
              "instructions": "How severe is this incident?",
              "criteria": "SEV4: no user impact, housekeeping\nSEV3: minor or internal impact, a workaround exists\nSEV2: a major feature is degraded for some customers\nSEV1: a core service is down or failing for most customers",
              "threshold": 0,
              "gate": true
            },
            {
              "key": "customer_facing",
              "type": "noul",
              "instructions": "Is this a customer-facing outage happening now?",
              "criteria": "yes: Customers cannot use part of the product right now\nno: Internal only, or a warning with no customer impact yet",
              "threshold": 0,
              "gate": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "threshold": 0.7,
        "additionalOptions": {
          "includeAudit": true
        }
      },
      "id": "635bcacf-dc01-5c25-a55e-07a022c2bcfb",
      "name": "Jev Decision",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-jev.jevDecision",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "typeSafeApi": {
          "id": "jevTypeSafeCred1",
          "name": "TypeSafe account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "8eada44f-db49-53fb-a2a9-88235cc26539",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.jev.answers.customer_facing.answer }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "b103aabb-625c-5835-ab9f-183fe090a20a",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.jev.answers.severity.level }}",
              "rightValue": 2,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gte"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "looseTypeValidation": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "6fa4217b-1ae1-597f-af3f-32594c7f8b23",
